        "original_id": "c4c05455-b6a6-5b66-9489-efed30d0336a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Chinese Crested Dog, Chien-gris, Mexican Hairless Dog\n- Concepts: hairless dog breeds, Powderpuff, Hairless, canine follicular dysplasia, alopecia\n\nFacts:\n- The Chien-gris, also called Gris de Saint-Louis or Grey St. Louis Hound, was a dog breed that originated in Medieval times and is now extinct.\n- The Chinese Crested Dog is a hairless breed of dog.\n- The Chinese Crested Dog has two varieties born in the same litter, the Powderpuff and the Hairless.\n- The Chinese Crested Dog is like most hairless dog breeds in having both furred and hairless varieties.\n- Certain dog breeds, including the Mexican Hairless Dog and the Chinese Crested Dog, are bred specifically for alopecia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
